### Product Inventory API - sample requests
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension and JetBrains HTTP Client.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@base = {{host}}/api/v1/products

### Health check
GET {{host}}/healthz

### Create a product
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "ProBook 15 Laptop",
  "sku": "LAP-PRO-15",
  "description": "15-inch laptop",
  "price": 1499.99,
  "stock_quantity": 12,
  "status": "active"
}

### Create with defaults (status=draft, stock_quantity=0)
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Minimal Product", "sku": "MIN-001", "price": 9.5 }

### Validation error (400): empty name, negative price, bad status
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "sku": "BAD-1", "price": -1, "status": "bogus" }

### Duplicate SKU (409) - run the first create twice
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Duplicate", "sku": "LAP-PRO-15", "price": 1 }

### Malformed JSON (400)
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name":

### List (defaults: page=1, page_size=10)
GET {{base}}

### List with pagination and status filter
GET {{base}}?page=1&page_size=5&status=active

### "limit" works as an alias for page_size
GET {{base}}?limit=3

### Bonus: search by name (case-insensitive, partial)
GET {{base}}?q=laptop

### Bonus: low stock (stock_quantity <= 5)
GET {{base}}?low_stock=true

### Get one product
GET {{base}}/1

### Invalid ID (400)
GET {{base}}/abc

### Not found (404)
GET {{base}}/999999

### Update (PUT) - only the supplied fields change
PUT {{base}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ProBook 15 Laptop (2026)", "price": 1399.00, "stock_quantity": 8 }

### Partial update (PATCH)
PATCH {{base}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "archived" }

### Change SKU to one that exists (409)
PUT {{base}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sku": "MIN-001" }

### Delete (204 No Content)
DELETE {{base}}/1
